-- ---- Further tests (Order 44) ----
-- Rule 4(6)(b), (c): which documents are required.  Arguments: the person under disability is a person lacking capacity; the proposer is authorised under the Act.
-- A person lacking capacity with an authorised deputy proposing: the sealed copy (b) is required, the Form 74 certificate (c) is not.
-- A person lacking capacity with no authorised proposer: (c) is required, (b) is not.  A minor (not lacking capacity): (c) is required, (b) is not.
#ASSERT `o 44 r 4(6)(b) a copy, sealed with the seal of the Court, of the order or other authorisation is required` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
